==Trivia==
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], [[Into the Future]]'s map lacks the blue tint that it has in all other versions of the game.
*The monkey-shaped crop circle on Into the Future's map is based on "The monkey", one of the many [[wikipedia:Nazca Lines|Nazca Lines]] of Peru.
*Some of the crop circles on Into the Future's map are shaped like the aliens from ''[[wikipedia:Space Invaders|Space Invaders]]''.
*[[Zero Field]]'s map looks like a red version of [[The Big Bang (Cats of the Cosmos)|The Big Bang]] from the [[Cats of the Cosmos]] map.
*The map of all 8 [[Zero Legends]] sub-chapters from [[The Edge of Spacetime]] through [[Garden of Wilted Thoughts]] is a jumbled up and mirrored map of Japan with real geographic features on it such as [[wikipedia:Mount Fuji|Mount Fuji]]. These 8 sub-chapters have a combined total of 48 stages, just like a [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapter]]; the 48th stage, [[Adherence to Virtue]], even has a unique [[Sage of Mind Soractes|boss]] and [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|reward]].
**These sub-chapters may specifically represent the Japanese version of [[Empire of Cats]], which takes place across the 47 prefectures of Japan and [[wikipedia:Iriomote Island|Iriomote Island]] rather than various countries and the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]].
*The map of all sub-chapters from [[Stratospheric Pathway]] through [[Truth's Devouring Maw]] is North and South America, but jumbled up and rearranged.
*The sub-chapters from [[A Journey of Moments]] through [[Eden of Evolution]] appear to take place in a flipped and reversed Eurasia with Italy turned into a lake and no Japan or [[wikipedia:Papua (province)|Papua]]. The floating islands on the map may be an homage to [[Floating Continent (Into the Future)|Floating Continent]], since the "final boss" of this part, [[Sage of Selection Darvin]], is an [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]], and the previous map has a [[Immeasurable Power|whirlpool]] resembling [[The Great Abyss (Into the Future)|The Great Abyss]].
**The omission of Japan is likely because The Edge of Spacetime through Garden of Wilted Thoughts already have a Japan-based map.
*The map used in [[New Horizon]] through [[Noodle Nirvana]] appears to be a flipped and reversed Australia, along with some other parts of Oceania and Indonesia.
*[[Pt. 1: A Decade of Memories]] shows [[Cats of the Cosmos]] before [[Heavenly Tower]], even though Heavenly Tower was added first. It also shows [[True Form]]s after [[Into the Future]], which is inaccurate unless referring to True Forms of [[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha units]] such as [[Megidora (Uber Rare Cat)|Megidora]].
*The map used in many of the [[Gauntlet]]s resembles a map of the Japanese city of Kyoto, especially the river.

